🥇 Gold Layer – Business-Ready Data Model

Implemented the Gold Layer as the final presentation layer of the Medallion Architecture, transforming the standardized Silver data into business-ready **dimension and fact views** for analytics and reporting.

What the code does:

`gold.dim_customers` – Customer Dimension

  * Creates a unique `customer_key` for analytics.
  * Combines CRM customer information with ERP demographic and location data.
  * Provides customer name, country, marital status, gender, birth date, and creation date.
  * Resolves gender using CRM data first and ERP data as a fallback.

`gold.dim_products` – Product Dimension

  * Creates a unique `product_key`.
  * Combines CRM product information with ERP product-category data.
  * Provides product, category, subcategory, maintenance, cost, product line, and start date.
  * Filters to the currently active product records.

`gold.fact_sales` – Sales Fact

  * Connects sales transactions with customer and product dimensions.
  * Provides order, product, customer, order/shipping/due dates, sales amount, quantity, and price.
  * Creates the central transactional dataset for sales analysis.

💼 Business Problems Solved

The Gold Layer converts technically complex source data into a simple analytical model that business users can query easily.

It enables:

* 📊 Sales performance analysis
* 👥 Customer segmentation and behavior analysis
* 📦 Product and category performance analysis
* 🌍 Geographic sales analysis
* 💰 Revenue and quantity analysis
* 📈 Trend analysis by date
* 🔗 Consistent integration of CRM and ERP data

The resulting Star Schema separates descriptive business entities (`dim_customers`, `dim_products`) from transactional metrics (`fact_sales`), making the warehouse easier to understand, query, and use for BI dashboards and reporting.

-- SQL CODE FOR GOLD LAYER

-- GOLD LAYER

CREATE VIEW gold.dim_customers AS
SELECT
	ROW_NUMBER() OVER(ORDER BY cst_id) AS customer_key,
	ci.cst_id AS customer_id,
	ci.cst_key AS customer_number,
	ci.cst_firstname AS first_name,
	ci.cst_lastname AS last_name,
	la.cntry AS country,
	ci.cst_marital_status AS marital_status,
	CASE WHEN ci.cst_gndr != 'n/a' THEN cst_gndr 
		 ELSE COALESCE(ca.gen,'n/a')
	END AS gender,
	ca.bdate AS birth_date,
	ci.cst_create_date AS create_date
FROM silver.crm_cust_info ci
LEFT JOIN silver.erp_CUST_AZ12 ca
ON ci.cst_key = ca.CID
LEFT JOIN silver.erp_LOC_A101 la
ON ci.cst_key = la.CID

CREATE VIEW gold.dim_products AS 
SELECT
	ROW_NUMBER() OVER(ORDER BY pn.prd_start_dt, pn.prd_key) AS product_key,
	pn.prd_id AS product_id,
	pn.prd_key AS product_number,
	pn.prd_nm AS product_name,
	pn.cat_id AS category_id,
	pc.CAT AS category,
	pc.SUBCAT AS subcategory,
	pc.MAINTENANCE AS Maintenance,
	pn.prd_cost AS product_cost,
	pn.prd_line AS product_line,
	pn.prd_start_dt AS start_date
FROM silver.crm_prd_info pn
LEFT JOIN silver.erp_PX_CAT_G1V2 pc
ON pn.cat_id = pc.ID
WHERE prd_end_dt IS NULL

CREATE VIEW gold.fact_sales AS
SELECT
	sd.sls_ord_num AS order_number,
	pr.product_key,
	cu.customer_key,
	sd.sls_order_dt AS order_date,
	sd.sls_ship_dt AS shipping_date,
	sd.sls_due_dt AS due_date,
	sd.sls_sales AS sales_amount,
	sd.sls_quantity AS quantity,
	sd.sls_price AS price
FROM silver.crm_sales_details sd
LEFT JOIN gold.dim_products pr
ON sd.sls_prd_key = pr.product_number
LEFT JOIN gold.dim_customers cu
ON sd.sls_cust_id = cu.customer_id
